Ruby client for the Printer interface. Debian does not package the Ice for Ruby
binding, install it with:

  $ sudo apt install ruby-dev g++ libssl-dev libbz2-dev
  $ sudo gem install zeroc-ice -v 3.7.10 -- --with-cflags="\
      -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration \
      -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types -Wno-error=int-conversion"

(the cflags are required to build it with GCC >= 14)

Run any Printer server, for example:

  py/hello$ make run-server

and then:

  ruby$ make run-client
